# Jarvis Stack (Latest Stable)

Pin **latest stable** versions at implementation time. Re-check crates.io / npm before adding deps.

## Rust / Tauri

| Component | Target |
|-----------|--------|
| Rust toolchain | `stable` (via `rustup`) |
| Edition | `2021` (workspace default) |
| Tauri | `2.x` latest stable (e.g. `tauri = "2.11"`, `tauri-build`, `tauri-cli` aligned) |
| SQLite | `rusqlite` with `bundled` + FTS5 |
| Vectors | `sqlite-vec` |
| Errors | `thiserror` |
| Async | `tokio` when needed |

## Frontend (Tauri webview)

| Component | Target |
|-----------|--------|
| React | latest stable |
| TypeScript | latest stable |
| Vite | latest stable |
| Tailwind | v4 (`@tailwindcss/vite` or `@tailwindcss/postcss`) |
| Animation | `motion` (`motion/react`) |
| Icons | `@phosphor-icons/react` or `@tabler/icons-react` |

## Policy

- Workspace layout: `src-tauri/` + `crates/*` + `src/` (React).
- Core logic in library crates; Tauri commands stay thin.
- No pinned pre-release unless required; document why if used.
- Upgrade deps deliberately; run full test suite after bumps.
